"title":"Śrī-Rūpa-Mañjarī-pada"}}},"song":{"meta":{"page":204,"first_line":"gopīnāth, āmāra upāya nāi","author":"Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"},"title":["Nivedana"],"author":["by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur"],"subtitle":["Part 3"],"verses":[{"number":"1","text":["gopīnāth,    āmāra upāya nāi","tumi kṛpā kori,    āmāre loile,","    saṁsāre udhāra pāi"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, I have no means of success, but if You take me, having bestowed Your mercy upon me, then I will obtain deliverance from this world."],"isLong":false},{"number":"2","text":["gopīnāth,    poḍechi māyāra phere","dhon, dārā, suta,    ghireche āmāre,","    kāmete rekheche jere"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, I have fallen into the perils of material illusion. Wealth, wife, and sons have surrounded me, and lust has wasted me away."],"isLong":false},{"number":"3","text":["gopīnāth,    mana je pāgala mora","nā māne śāsana,    sadā achetana,","    viṣoye royeche bhora"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, my mind is crazy and does not care for any authority. It is always senseless and has remained in the dark pit of worldly affairs."],"isLong":false},{"number":"4","text":["gopīnāth,    hāra je menechi āmi","oneka jatana,    hoilo biphala,","    ekhona bharasā tumi"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, I have accepted my defeat. All of my various endeavours were useless. Now You are the only hope."],"isLong":false},{"number":"5","text":["gopīnāth,    kemone hoibe gati","prabala indriya,    bośī-bhūta mana,","    nā chāḍe viṣoya-rati"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, how shall I make any advancement when my mind has come under the control of the powerful senses and does not abandon its attachment to materialism?"],"isLong":false},{"number":"6","text":["gopīnāth,    hṛdoye bosiyā mora","manake śamiyā,    loho nija pāne,","    ghuchibe vipada ghora"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, after sitting down in the core of my heart and subduing my mind, please take me to You. In this way the horrible dangers of this world will disappear."],"isLong":false},{"number":"7","text":["gopīnāth,    anātha dekhiyā more","tumi hṛṣīkeśa,    hṛṣīka damiyā,","    tāro’ he saṁsṛti-ghore"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, You are Hṛṣīkeśa, the Lord of the senses. Seeing me so helpless, please control these senses of mine and deliver me from this dark and perilous worldly existence."],"isLong":false},{"number":"8","text":["gopīnāth,    golāya legeche phā̐sa","kṛpā-asi dhori,    bandhana chediyā,","    vinode karaho dāsa"],"translation":["Oh Gopīnāth, the noose of materialism has become fixed around my neck. Taking up the sword of Your mercy and cutting this bondage, make this Bhakti Vinod Your humble servant."],"isLong":false}],"resources":{"audio":[{"title":"Manasa Krishna Prabhu","embed_url":"https://soundcloud.com/huron/gopinath-amara-upaya-nai","personSlug":"manasa-krishna-prabhu"}]},"hasWbw":false,"hasVersesText":true,"hasVersesTranslations":true,"hasLongVerses":false,"fullInlineWbw":false},"telegraphUrl":null},"head":{"canonical":"/en-2022/gopinath-amara-upaya-nai/","description":"Nivedana — a Vaiṣṇava song by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur with lyrics, English translation and word-by-word meaning. From Kirtan Guide.","title":"Nivedana. by Śrīla Bhakti Vinod Ṭhākur. Part 3 | Kirtan Site"},"kind":"song","route":{"kind":"item","bookId":"en-2022","slug":"gopinath-amara-upaya-nai"}}